00:17:01.820 --> 00:17:03.940
Gee, Dad's never been a hittin' father.

00:17:04.740 --> 00:17:07.680
I know. But if he's ever gonna be one, this oughta do it.

00:17:09.150 --> 00:17:12.560
Yeah. Maybe I oughta go in and tell Mom what I did.

00:17:13.240 --> 00:17:17.060
You know, she might soften Dad up. Tell him I'm just a little kid and all that.

00:17:17.940 --> 00:17:22.630
I don't know, babe. Sometimes when you tell Mother stuff like that, they start to cry.

00:17:23.820 --> 00:17:27.600
Yeah. Gee, I'd rather be yelled at than cried at.

00:17:36.140 --> 00:17:38.140
Beaver, we've been looking for you.

00:17:39.030 --> 00:17:41.650
Mrs. Rayburn sent for your father to come down to the school.

00:17:42.560 --> 00:17:42.780
Oh?

00:17:43.160 --> 00:17:43.860
Do you know why?

00:17:44.840 --> 00:17:46.120
I guess she wanted to talk to him.

00:17:46.970 --> 00:17:50.090
I know that. Do you know why she wanted to talk to him?

00:17:51.630 --> 00:17:52.610
Something pretty bad.

00:17:53.930 --> 00:17:54.490
How bad?

00:17:55.830 --> 00:17:57.130
It's almost running away bad.

00:17:58.410 --> 00:17:59.470
Beaver, what'd you do?

00:18:00.540 --> 00:18:04.390
Well, when they took the class picture, I made a face and ruined it.

00:18:05.800 --> 00:18:06.800
You made a face?

00:18:07.710 --> 00:18:08.470
Yeah, like this.

00:18:11.050 --> 00:18:12.950
Oh, Beaver, how could you?

00:18:13.810 --> 00:18:18.330
Well, I plan to send those pictures to Aunt Martha and Uncle Billy and all our relatives.

00:18:19.490 --> 00:18:22.010
Beaver, I'm just so disappointed I don't know what to do.

00:18:24.840 --> 00:18:26.180
Please don't start crying, Mom.

00:18:26.750 --> 00:18:27.890
I'll do anything you want me to.

00:18:27.970 --> 00:18:29.710
I'll even kill myself if you don't start crying.

00:18:31.440 --> 00:18:34.340
No, Beaver, I just can't believe you'd do a thing like this.

00:18:34.840 --> 00:18:38.990
I just can't believe Theodore would do a thing like this.

00:18:39.630 --> 00:18:43.390
You can see, Mr. Cleaver, you spoiled the whole class picture.

00:18:44.240 --> 00:18:46.560
We really can't understand it, Mr. Cleaver.

00:18:47.100 --> 00:18:50.040
Theodore usually shows a pretty good sense of responsibility.

00:18:51.390 --> 00:18:52.930
He certainly isn't showing one here.

00:18:53.350 --> 00:18:57.010
What makes it so serious is that the yearbook has gone to press,

00:18:57.150 --> 00:18:59.880
so the picture will have to go in just this way.

00:19:00.410 --> 00:19:05.320
Yes. Well, I guess it's going to be quite embarrassing for all of us.

00:19:05.720 --> 00:19:08.900
Oh, we're used to boys that play pranks now and then.

00:19:09.140 --> 00:19:11.590
But it's what this implies, Mr. Cleaver.

00:19:12.050 --> 00:19:16.350
It shows the other students that Theodore has no respect for his school,

00:19:16.350 --> 00:19:18.770
his classmates, that it's just one big joke.

00:19:19.820 --> 00:19:21.920
Well, I can assure you, Mrs. Rayburn, when I get home,

00:19:21.980 --> 00:19:24.280
I'll make it very clear to him that this isn't a joke.

00:19:24.620 --> 00:19:27.040
And I'm certainly going to speak to him in class tomorrow.

00:19:28.020 --> 00:19:29.980
Well, I'm just awfully...

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:32.930
Sorry, I don't know what his mother's going to think of it.

00:19:33.500 --> 00:19:37.100
I'm wondering what the superintendent of schools is going to think of us.

00:19:39.720 --> 00:19:42.780
Well, Ward, can't the school just tear up the picture?

00:19:43.280 --> 00:19:46.070
Oh, you're going to have to print it, just as it is.

00:19:47.330 --> 00:19:49.870
Well, this family hasn't moved in a long time.

00:19:50.250 --> 00:19:51.510
Guess we better start packing.

00:19:51.930 --> 00:19:53.190
Wally, you're not helping.

00:19:54.050 --> 00:19:55.540
Oh, I'm sorry, Dad.

00:19:56.090 --> 00:19:58.070
Ward, Beaver showed me the face he made.

00:19:58.350 --> 00:19:59.530
How bad was it in the picture?

00:20:00.410 --> 00:20:04.580
Well, do you remember how a happy hooligan used to look in the funny papers?

00:20:05.240 --> 00:20:06.100
I'm afraid not.

00:20:07.040 --> 00:20:09.000
Good, because that's just who he looks like.

00:20:09.480 --> 00:20:10.320
Where is he now?

00:20:11.050 --> 00:20:13.480
He's upstairs. I think he's got the door lot.

00:20:14.180 --> 00:20:15.800
Go up and have this out with him right now.

00:20:15.980 --> 00:20:19.040
Dear, dear, don't be too hard on him.

00:20:19.430 --> 00:20:21.250
Now, don't forget, he's just a little boy.

00:20:21.670 --> 00:20:29.180
You know, Mom, Dad doesn't have to get so steamed up about the beaver.

00:20:29.820 --> 00:20:29.980
He can...

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:31.640
just let the school give him the business.

00:20:32.640 --> 00:20:34.860
Well, now, Wally, we can't turn all of our problems

00:20:34.860 --> 00:20:35.920
over to the school.

00:20:36.770 --> 00:20:39.490
Your father feels that the parents should be responsible

00:20:39.490 --> 00:20:41.190
for the discipline of the children.

00:20:42.080 --> 00:20:44.400
Yeah. I guess if a kid's gonna get hit,

00:20:44.920 --> 00:20:46.640
it's better if he gets hit by his own parents.

00:20:47.480 --> 00:20:51.500
Who is it?

00:20:52.150 --> 00:20:52.810
Your father.

00:20:54.880 --> 00:20:55.240
Father?

00:20:57.320 --> 00:20:59.220
Come on, son. Open up.

00:21:00.510 --> 00:21:01.170
Yes, sir.

00:21:08.010 --> 00:21:10.110
Well, Beaver, I just came from Mrs. Rayburn's office,

00:21:10.130 --> 00:21:13.690
and I saw the class picture they took the other day with you making the face.

00:21:15.760 --> 00:21:17.120
Are we gonna have to pay for a new one, Dad?

00:21:17.300 --> 00:21:18.420
It's too late for a new one.

00:21:18.730 --> 00:21:20.870
It has to go in the yearbook just the way it is.

00:21:21.540 --> 00:21:24.110
Boy, I'm gonna feel real creepy when it comes out.

00:21:24.820 --> 00:21:26.980
Well, Beaver, how do you think your mother and I are going to feel?

00:21:27.570 --> 00:21:29.960
And Miss Landers and Mrs. Rayburn, they're going to...

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:31.560
You're going to be embarrassed for the whole school.

00:21:32.480 --> 00:21:34.740
And what about the parents of the other children in your class?

00:21:35.300 --> 00:21:37.860
How do you think they're going to feel when they see you've ruined the picture?

00:21:38.680 --> 00:21:41.380
Gee, Dad, I thought I was just going to get myself in trouble.

00:21:41.880 --> 00:21:44.300
Now it looks like practically the whole world's going to be mad at me.

00:21:44.800 --> 00:21:47.560
When you do something wrong, Beaver, or break a rule,

00:21:47.800 --> 00:21:50.400
it can affect and hurt a lot of people.

00:21:50.670 --> 00:21:53.410
Gee, Dad, if I would know it was going to happen before it happened,

00:21:53.610 --> 00:21:56.240
I wouldn't have done it. What I mean is I'm sorry.

00:21:57.650 --> 00:21:58.510
Oh, well, that's fine.

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:02.660
But will you please tell me why you did it?

00:22:03.160 --> 00:22:06.480
Well, the guy said if I made a face, he'd make a face.

00:22:06.960 --> 00:22:09.180
And then when I took the picture, he didn't make a face.

00:22:11.820 --> 00:22:12.800
I'm not surprised.

00:22:14.180 --> 00:22:15.440
Well, I did. Do you know the guy?

00:22:17.420 --> 00:22:18.080
No, Beaver.

00:22:18.390 --> 00:22:21.150
But I do know that when a person comes up with a bad idea,

00:22:21.330 --> 00:22:23.430
he's usually the first one to double-cross you.

00:22:24.090 --> 00:22:26.170
I thought it'd be neat if we both made a face together.

00:22:26.790 --> 00:22:29.070
Wasn't so neat when he left you holding the bag, was it?

00:22:30.030 --> 00:22:33.900
No, sir. What are you going to do to me, Dad?

00:22:35.000 --> 00:22:38.000
Well, first of all, you're going to apologize to Miss Landers and Mrs. Rayburn.

00:22:38.640 --> 00:22:43.030
And I think you'd better come home right after school for the next week.

00:22:43.980 --> 00:22:45.640
And don't make any plans for the weekend.

00:22:46.570 --> 00:22:48.770
Gee, Dad, you mean I've grown up for a whole week?

00:22:49.640 --> 00:22:50.140
That's right.

00:22:51.680 --> 00:22:55.350
Boy, Dad, if this would have happened about three years ago,

00:22:55.550 --> 00:22:56.850
you would have spanked me, wouldn't you?

00:22:57.010 --> 00:22:58.230
Yes, Beaver, I might have.

00:22:58.780 --> 00:22:59.980
But I think you're old enough to read...

00:23:00.910 --> 00:23:03.720
Yeah, I guess when you think about it,

00:23:04.000 --> 00:23:05.340
one's just as bad as the other.

00:23:13.060 --> 00:23:17.600
Eddie, Eddie, come in. Over.

00:23:20.720 --> 00:23:23.890
Eddie, will you please come in? Over.

00:23:27.720 --> 00:23:28.360
Oh, hi, Beef.

00:23:30.250 --> 00:23:36.790
thing working yet? Well, I got some guy on a little while ago. Was it daddy? Nah, it was this

00:23:37.230 --> 00:23:42.460
exterminator guy. He was telling one of his drivers where to go next and kill bugs. Hey,

00:23:43.710 --> 00:23:53.350
you want to see my class yearbook? Well, yeah. There's our class. Hey, where's you with the

00:23:53.350 --> 00:23:56.590
goofy face? Here I am, right behind Myrtle Jarvis.

00:24:00.700 --> 00:24:01.420
Well, what happened?

00:24:02.170 --> 00:24:04.370
Well, Mr. Baxter, the photographer, got an idea.

00:24:04.760 --> 00:24:07.480
He painted Myrtle's hair even bigger, so he'd cover my goofy face.

00:24:08.060 --> 00:24:09.640
Hey, that was pretty neat of him.

00:24:10.050 --> 00:24:12.210
Now your goofy face isn't crumbling up the whole picture.

00:24:13.150 --> 00:24:18.430
Yeah, I've been thinking, Wally.

00:24:18.930 --> 00:24:20.610
What's gonna happen when I get kids of my own?

00:24:21.540 --> 00:24:22.980
They're gonna come up to me and they're gonna say,

00:24:23.840 --> 00:24:26.350
Hey, Beaver, what'd you look like when you were a kid?

00:24:26.630 --> 00:24:28.030
I don't have anything to show them.

00:24:28.890 --> 00:24:29.910
Wait a minute, Beaver.

00:24:30.480 --> 00:24:33.300
In the first place, your kids aren't going to call you Beaver.

00:24:33.720 --> 00:24:35.120
No? What'll they call me?

00:24:35.640 --> 00:24:37.120
They'll call you Dad. What else?

00:24:37.700 --> 00:24:42.080
Boy, if a kid ever called me Dad, I'd be so scared I wouldn't know what to do.

00:24:42.640 --> 00:24:46.380
No, you wouldn't. You'd probably feel creepy at first.

00:24:46.600 --> 00:24:48.740
Then you'd get used to it like our Dad did.

00:24:50.170 --> 00:24:51.640
Yeah, I guess so.

00:24:57.840 --> 00:24:58.280
Hello, Eddie.

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:01.400
Eddie, come in.

00:25:30.320 --> 00:25:30.560
Thank you.
